nak|a|Soon; in good season; seasonably; betimes; as, come early. ; In advance of the usual or appointed time; in good season; prior in time; among or near the first; -- opposed to late; as, the early bird; an early spring; early fruit. ; Coming in the first part of a period of time, or among the first of successive acts, events, etc.	j:1yzq,84,6;1yzg,75,23;b13,67,38;i9y,54,16;2bj5,26,6;16eq,24,5;1hdy,19,5~b13,67,38;1yzg,75,23;i9y,54,16;2bj5,26,6;1yzq,84,6;16eq,24,5;1hdy,19,5	e:2911,22,20;29of,12,1~2911,22,20;29of,12,1
